  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25616858",
      "title": "Working with MongoDB",
      "sourceHash": "2e5d96a4af79faf7d9b0622c3081559011d673be8bcaec4d2517b2ccb36a27a0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.81,
          "en": "Now, as a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.81,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "I will use MongoDB here and to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 10.98,
          "en": "I'll use their cloud offering, MongoDB Atlas,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.98,
          "end": 15.05,
          "en": "which is a fully managed cloud-based MongoDB database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.05,
          "end": 18.6,
          "en": "with which we can get started for free.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.6,
          "end": 21.26,
          "en": "All you need to do is click Try Free.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.26,
          "end": 24.9,
          "en": "This will then get you to MongoDB Atlas in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 27.9,
          "en": "and create an account for free here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.9,
          "end": 30.17,
          "en": "So just enter some data about yourself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.17,
          "end": 32.063,
          "en": "and then get started for free.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.9,
          "end": 34.348,
          "en": "If you do all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.348,
          "end": 37.1,
          "en": "after logging in, you'll end up on a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.1,
          "end": 39.27,
          "en": "where you can create a new cluster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.27,
          "end": 41.54,
          "en": "You must also automatically end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.54,
          "end": 44.28,
          "en": "in that create a cluster wizard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.28,
          "end": 47.68,
          "en": "And here you can generally leave all the settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.68,
          "end": 48.55,
          "en": "as they are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.55,
          "end": 52.1,
          "en": "Just make sure that you always pick the free tier settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.1,
          "end": 54.14,
          "en": "unless you wanna pay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.14,
          "end": 56.52,
          "en": "So for example, you can go with AWS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 58.37,
          "en": "and the default region here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.37,
          "end": 61.85,
          "en": "And leave all the other default settings as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.85,
          "end": 66.054,
          "en": "Especially make sure that you're using the M0 Sandbox here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.054,
          "end": 68.23,
          "en": "I can't select this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.23,
          "end": 71.38,
          "en": "because I already do have a cluster created based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.38,
          "end": 74.77,
          "en": "on that sandbox but if you don't have a cluster yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.77,
          "end": 78.4,
          "en": "you should be able to select M0 Sandbox.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.4,
          "end": 81.59,
          "en": "And that is the cluster tier you should use then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.59,
          "end": 84.03999999999999,
          "en": "And then just leave all the other default settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.03999999999999,
          "end": 85.7,
          "en": "and create your cluster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.7,
          "end": 90,
          "en": "Again, I already have one based on that M0 Sandbox here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90,
          "end": 93.53999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore, you eventually should also have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 97.16,
          "en": "Now, that's the cluster, the MongoDB database cluster,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.16,
          "end": 99.12,
          "en": "which we'll use to connect to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.12,
          "end": 101.34,
          "en": "to then create our database in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.34,
          "end": 103.173,
          "en": "and to store our data in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.12,
          "end": 106.85,
          "en": "Now, in order to be able to connect to this cluster,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.85,
          "end": 109.16,
          "en": "there are two things you also have to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.16,
          "end": 111.68,
          "en": "in this MongoDB Atlas console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.68,
          "end": 113.37,
          "en": "Under Network Access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 116.16,
          "en": "you have to add your local IP here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 118.00999999999999,
          "en": "by clicking on Add IP Address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.00999999999999,
          "end": 120.38,
          "en": "and then selecting current IP",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.38,
          "end": 123.4,
          "en": "so that your local computer is able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.4,
          "end": 126.69,
          "en": "to send requests to MongoDB",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 128.96,
          "en": "and under Database Access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.96,
          "end": 131.8,
          "en": "you need to create at least one user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 131.8,
          "end": 134.18,
          "en": "with any username of your choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 134.18,
          "end": 137.583,
          "en": "who has to have read and write access to the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 137.583,
          "end": 139.542,
          "en": "like this user here does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 139.542,
          "end": 143.18,
          "en": "so that this is a user with which we can connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.18,
          "end": 144.633,
          "en": "to this cluster later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.27,
          "end": 148.2,
          "en": "And once you did all of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.2,
          "end": 150.53,
          "en": "on Clusters, you can click on Connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.53,
          "end": 152.47,
          "en": "and then connect your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.47,
          "end": 155.543,
          "en": "to learn how you can connect to this cluster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.13,
          "end": 158.73,
          "en": "And here we now actually need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.73,
          "end": 162.11,
          "en": "to use the Node.js MongoDB driver",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 162.11,
          "end": 165.77,
          "en": "to write code here in our APIi route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 165.77,
          "end": 169.883,
          "en": "that does send queries to this MongoDB Atlas cluster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.91,
          "end": 173.42000000000002,
          "en": "For this, we need to quit the development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 173.42000000000002,
          "end": 177.16,
          "en": "and install an extra package with npm install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 177.16,
          "end": 180.033,
          "en": "The mongodb package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.87,
          "end": 182.93,
          "en": "This is the official MongoDB driver,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 182.93,
          "end": 186.42,
          "en": "which makes sending queries to MongoDB easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 187.37,
          "en": "Once you install it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 187.37,
          "end": 190.52,
          "en": "you can start the development server again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 190.52,
          "end": 193.51,
          "en": "And now this MongoDB driver allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 193.51,
          "end": 195.73,
          "en": "to connect to this cluster",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 195.73,
          "end": 199.743,
          "en": "and then insert data or fetch data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 200.66,
          "end": 202.86,
          "en": "For this in this api route file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 202.86,
          "end": 207.86,
          "en": "we can import something from mongodb",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.77,
          "end": 213.427,
          "en": "and that something is the MongoClient object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 216.78,
          "end": 219.84,
          "en": "This is our object which allows us to connect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 219.84,
          "end": 221.3,
          "en": "We can execute this code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.3,
          "end": 224.713,
          "en": "We can use MongoClient and call the connect method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.92000000000002,
          "end": 228.77,
          "en": "Now, the connect method wants this connection string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228.77,
          "end": 230.09,
          "en": "which we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.09,
          "end": 232.36,
          "en": "So you should copy that string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.36,
          "end": 235.82,
          "en": "and then pass this as a parameter here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.82,
          "end": 237.03300000000002,
          "en": "to the connect method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 240.57,
          "en": "Now, there, you need to plug in the username",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.57,
          "end": 243.17,
          "en": "and password of your user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 243.17,
          "end": 246.25,
          "en": "So that user who has read and write access,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 246.25,
          "end": 247.343,
          "en": "which you created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.1,
          "end": 252.22,
          "en": "And I'll quickly do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.22,
          "end": 256.27,
          "en": "without the angle brackets like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.27,
          "end": 258.48,
          "en": "Now, I will have changed my password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.48,
          "end": 259.5,
          "en": "when you're viewing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.5,
          "end": 262.773,
          "en": "so you don't need to try to connect to my cluster.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 264.12,
          "end": 267.35,
          "en": "You also should replace myFirstDatabase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 267.35,
          "end": 271.5,
          "en": "with any database name of your choice, for example, meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.5,
          "end": 272.713,
          "en": "but that is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.21,
          "end": 278.1,
          "en": "Now, when you do that, connect will establish a connection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 278.1,
          "end": 282.44,
          "en": "And this is code which you never, never want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.44,
          "end": 284.43,
          "en": "to run on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 284.43,
          "end": 288.1,
          "en": "because you would expose your credentials to your visitors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 288.1,
          "end": 290.8,
          "en": "which is a security problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 290.8,
          "end": 293.45,
          "en": "But here in this API route, it's no problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.45,
          "end": 295.48,
          "en": "because as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 295.48,
          "end": 297.45,
          "en": "the code defined in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 297.45,
          "end": 300.4,
          "en": "will never end up on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 300.4,
          "end": 304.293,
          "en": "so this is a secure place to store credentials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 305.76,
          "end": 308.5,
          "en": "Now, connect does return a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 308.5,
          "end": 311.3,
          "en": "and hence, we can turn our handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 311.3,
          "end": 314.61,
          "en": "into a async function to use await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 314.61,
          "end": 318.62,
          "en": "This is possible and supported by NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 318.62,
          "end": 321.963,
          "en": "And then this will give us a connected client eventually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 323.56,
          "end": 327.01,
          "en": "Now, on that client object, we can all the db method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 327.01,
          "end": 331.36,
          "en": "to get hold of that database to which we're connecting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 331.36,
          "end": 334.2,
          "en": "By the way, if that database doesn't exist yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 334.2,
          "end": 336.173,
          "en": "it will be created on the fly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 337.1,
          "end": 338.78,
          "en": "And then on this database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 338.78,
          "end": 341.563,
          "en": "we can get access to our meetupsCollection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 343.1,
          "end": 346.76,
          "en": "Now, MongoDB is a NoSQL database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 346.76,
          "end": 351,
          "en": "that works with collections full of documents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 351,
          "end": 354.90999999999997,
          "en": "Collections would be kind of your tables in a SQL database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 354.90999999999997,
          "end": 359.43,
          "en": "and documents would be your entries in those tables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 359.43,
          "end": 360.76,
          "en": "So you have collections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.76,
          "end": 363.01,
          "en": "which hold multiple documents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.01,
          "end": 366.38,
          "en": "And a single meetup would be a single document,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 366.38,
          "end": 370.3,
          "en": "the overall collection then holds multiple meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 370.3,
          "end": 371.853,
          "en": "multiple meetup documents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 372.72,
          "end": 375.59,
          "en": "And you get hold of a collection by using your database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 375.59,
          "end": 377.92,
          "en": "and then the collection method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 377.92,
          "end": 380.96,
          "en": "And the collection can have any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 380.96,
          "end": 384,
          "en": "Just as the database if it doesn't exist yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 384,
          "end": 386.58,
          "en": "it will be generated on the fly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 386.58,
          "end": 388.563,
          "en": "And it could be named meetups as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 389.46,
          "end": 392.18,
          "en": "So it can have the same name as the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 392.18,
          "end": 394.563,
          "en": "but you can also use different names here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 396.36,
          "end": 399.274,
          "en": "And now that we got hold of the meetupsCollection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 399.274,
          "end": 403.06,
          "en": "on that collection here, we can call insertOne,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 403.06,
          "end": 405.3,
          "en": "which is one of the built-in query commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 405.3,
          "end": 409.83,
          "en": "for inserting one new document into this collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 409.83,
          "end": 411.99,
          "en": "And now the great thing about MongoDB",
